  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday)\nIssued at 224 AM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nThe upper ridge is forecast to flatten and move east towards the end \nof the week into the weekend as troughing across the west coast \ndeepens. This will help bend the subtropical moisture plume eastward \ninto our area and allow for increasing shower/storm chances across \nwestern OK and western north TX Thursday night into Friday, with \nchances then expanding across more of the area as we head into \nSaturday and Sunday. That said, veering/drying flow and weakening\nforcing may lead to dwindling shower/storm coverage as activity \nmakes it into central/eastern parts of the area. \n\nTemperatures will remain well above average through the end of \nthis forecast period, with highs climbing above 90 degrees \nareawide, with some portions of southern OK into western north TX \npotentially getting back close to the 100 degree mark, especially \nif shower/storm coverage ends up more limited. \n\nWare",
